# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, or add these as
# Environment Variables in your Vercel project settings for production.

# --- Site URL (recommended for production) --------------------------------
# Used to build absolute URLs in metadata, the sitemap, robots.txt and
# structured data (Organization/PodcastEpisode/NewsArticle JSON-LD). Set
# this to your real deployed domain (e.g. https://tygcp.org, or your
# *.vercel.app URL before a custom domain is attached) — no trailing slash.
# Falls back to a placeholder domain if unset, which is fine for local
# development but should always be set in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --- Database (required for form submissions to be saved) ---------------
# PHASE 3 BATCH 1: this project now runs on PostgreSQL — SQLite never worked
# on Vercel's serverless filesystem (each invocation gets an ephemeral disk),
# so this replaces the Phase 2 local-only SQLite setup everywhere, including
# local development. You need a real Postgres database, even to run `npm run
# dev` locally. See README.md "Database" for full setup steps.
#
# PRISMA 7 CORRECTIVE UPDATE: the running app now connects through
# @prisma/adapter-neon (see src/lib/db.ts), which speaks Neon's own
# HTTP/WebSocket protocol rather than a generic Postgres TCP connection.
# That means DATABASE_URL must point at a real Neon endpoint — either Neon
# directly, or Vercel Postgres (which runs on Neon under the hood) — not a
# generic/self-hosted Postgres instance or Supabase; those speak the
# standard Postgres wire protocol, not Neon's, and would need
# @prisma/adapter-pg instead (a small, documented swap in src/lib/db.ts, not
# a schema change) if you ever move off Neon.
#
# Two variables, not one — see the datasource comment at the top of
# prisma/schema.prisma and prisma.config.ts for the full reasoning:
#   DATABASE_URL — the connection the running app uses for every query.
#     Use your Neon project's POOLED connection string here (the one with
#     "-pooler" in the hostname).
#   DIRECT_URL   — used only by the Prisma CLI (`prisma generate`, `prisma
#     migrate`, ...), never by the running app. Use your Neon project's
#     DIRECT (unpooled) connection string here.
# Both must still be set to *something*, or `prisma generate` (including the
# `postinstall` step that runs after `npm install`) will fail with
# "Environment variable not found."
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=

# --- Admin dashboard (required to sign in at /admin) ---------------------
# A single shared password gates /admin for now — see README.md "Admin
# dashboard" for why this is a deliberate Phase-2 scope decision, and what
# real multi-user/role-based auth (Phase 3) would replace it with.
# Generate a strong value, e.g.: openssl rand -base64 24
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Used to sign the admin session cookie. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Email notifications (optional) ---------------------------------------
# Without these, form submissions are still saved to the database (above)
# and logged to the server console, but nobody is emailed automatically.
# See the "Email" section of README.md.
RESEND_API_KEY=
NOTIFY_TO_EMAIL=
